cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this code or these results, please cite the paper below."
title: "Component Type, Not Reconstruction Error, Predicts Attention Quantization Sensitivity"
abstract: >-
  We quantize one attention projection at a time across nine open-weight language models
  (1.3B-8B parameters) under RTN and GPTQ at 3 and 4 bits, recording reconstruction error,
  perplexity change, and activation-weighted quantization error for 3,808 distinct
  measurements. Reconstruction error is a weak within-component predictor of perplexity
  sensitivity (median R^2 = 0.044); component type and layer identity both carry more
  information; V projections dominate in seven of nine models; and activation-weighted
  quantization error is a substantially better V-projection predictor.
type: software
